@param threadId: String
@param summoning: Boolean = true
@if(summoning)
    <%-- "Summoning the room…": the create-time room summon is still routing on a worker (the dispatcher's
         "who replies" LLM call). Self-polls GET /threads/{id}/room every second. While routing is still in
         flight that endpoint re-emits this poller, which replaces ONLY ITSELF — so a note the owner posts
         mid-wait keeps its place on the page. Once routing has concluded it answers with whatever the room
         produced (drafts still in flight, replies that already settled, or both), retargeting the whole
         reply list so the server render replaces it wholesale and this poller goes with it; a summon that
         ended having produced nothing emits nothing, so htmx stops either way.
         data-empty-state mirrors the static "waiting" state's hook. --%>
    <div data-empty-state="summoning"
         hx-get="/threads/${threadId}/room"
         hx-trigger="every 1s"
         hx-swap="outerHTML">Summoning the room…</div>
@endif
